        </h2>
        <p>
          To harvest positive funding yields without exposing capital to underlying price volatility, a quant establishes a <strong>Cash-and-Carry Delta-Neutral Pair</strong>:
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 font-mono text-xs my-4">
          <div class="bg-[#080E1C] p-5 rounded-xl border border-slate-800">
            <h3 class="text-emerald-400 font-bold text-sm mb-2">Leg 1: Spot Asset Purchase</h3>
            <p>&bull; Capital Allocated: \$50,000 USD</p>
            <p>&bull; Asset Bought: 16.66 ETH at \$3,000 spot</p>
            <p>&bull; Delta Contribution: <strong>+16.66 ETH</strong> (Long)</p>
            <p>&bull; Custody: On-chain cold wallet or exchange spot</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-[#080E1C] p-5 rounded-xl border border-slate-800">
            <h3 class="text-cyan-400 font-bold text-sm mb-2">Leg 2: Perpetual Futures Short</h3>
            <p>&bull; Capital Allocated: \$50,000 USDC Margin</p>
            <p>&bull; Contract: Short 16.66 ETH-PERP at \$3,005</p>
            <p>&bull; Delta Contribution: <strong>-16.66 ETH</strong> (Short)</p>
            <p>&bull; Effective Leverage: 1.0x (Zero borrowed margin)</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p>
          <strong>Total Combined Delta:</strong> &Delta;<sub>net</sub> = (+16.66) + (-16.66) = <strong>0.00</strong>. If ETH doubles to $6,000, the spot leg gains $50,000 while the short perp loses $50,000. If ETH drops to $1,500, the spot leg loses $25,000 while the short perp gains $25,000. Directional price risk is neutralized.
        </p>
        <div class="bg-slate-950 p-3 rounded-lg font-mono text-xs text-center border border-slate-800 text-emerald-300 my-2">
          Payout = Position Notional &times; Funding Rate = $50,000 &times; 0.03% = +$15.00 cash
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 4: Liquidation Defense & Margin Health Factor -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-rose-400"></span>
          <span>4. Liquidation Risk Mitigation &amp; Margin Health Factors</span>
        </h2>
        <p>
          Although the portfolio is delta-neutral in aggregate, the short perpetual leg resides on a margin exchange. If the spot asset rallies parabolically, the unrealized loss on the short position can trigger margin calls or catastrophic liquidation if unmanaged.
        </p>

        <pre is:raw class="bg-[#0A101D] border border-slate-800 p-4 rounded-xl font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm text-rose-300 overflow-x-auto">
Liquidation Price Estimate (1x Leverage, 100% Collateral):
P_liq = Entry_Price * (1 + (Collateral / Notional) - Maintenance_Margin_Rate)

For Entry = $3,000, Collateral = $50,000, Notional = $50,000, MMR = 0.5%:
P_liq = $3,000 * (1 + 1.0 - 0.005) = $5,985 (+99.5% rally headroom)
        </pre>

        <div class="bg-[#080E1C] p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-800 space-y-2 text-xs">
          <h4 class="font-bold text-white uppercase font-mono">Institutional Liquidation Protocol Rules:</h4>
          <p>&bull; <strong>Rebalancing Threshold:</strong> If asset appreciation reduces perp margin equity below 35%, automatically transfer spot profits to collateral or downsize 20% of both legs.</p>
          <p>&bull; <strong>Negative Funding Circuit Breaker:</strong> If 72-hour cumulative funding turns negative ($&lt; -0.015\%$), close the short perp and liquidate the spot leg to prevent capital bleed.</p>
          <p>&bull; <strong>Execution Slip Minimization:</strong> Utilize TWAP (Time-Weighted Average Price) algorithmic orders to enter both spot and perpetual legs simultaneously, avoiding front-running slippage.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- CTA Card -->
      <div class="bg-gradient-to-br from-[#0C1527] to-[#0A101D] border border-indigo-500/30 p-8 rounded-2xl text-center space-y-4 shadow-xl">
